<%#
  One public project on a list — /u/:handle and /explore share it, which is what keeps the two
  from drifting about what a project looks like. Every link is public: the project page, the
  maker's page, and each tag's /explore filter.

  Locals: project (Maker::Project, publicly listed), thumb (Maker::Preview or nil).
%>
<article class="grid-card project-card">
  <%#
    THE COVER (stage 4, S4-5; story 5.7). `thumb` is a Maker::Preview or nil — the private
    projects/_card's shape, minus the poll: /files/thumbnails is session-authed, so a visitor's
    spinner has nothing that could ever resolve it. A card with no cover node gets the same neutral
    placeholder the private card uses, never a forever-spinner.

    `thumb` IS ALLOWED TO BE nil AND /explore ALWAYS PASSES nil (this slice's Amendment 9).
    Maker::Previews::ThumbnailMap is PER-USER, so a cross-user list would cost three statements per
    distinct maker — measured by page_query_budget_test.rb, whose explore seed mints one owner per
    project because that is what /explore is. This is ONE condition (does this card have a ready
    cover thumbnail?) answered from whatever each caller actually holds, not two answers to one
    condition.
  %>
  <%= link_to public_project_path(project.user.handle, project.slug), class: "card-cover" do %>
    <%# THE PUBLIC PREVIEW ROUTE, NEVER `url_for(thumb.asset)` (hardening, 2026-09-08;
        tinkerex#278). A blob URL is unauthenticated and never expires, so this card's cover kept
        answering after its project went private — the route asks `Maker::PublicProject#deliverable!`
        per request instead and redirects to a service URL that lives five minutes. `thumb` is a
        Maker::Preview, which carries the `node_id` the route needs, so no extra local. NO `k`
        TOKEN: a card only ever renders for a `publicly_listed` project, and an unlisted one is
        excluded from both lists by the scope above this partial. %>
    <% if thumb&.status == "ready" && thumb.asset.attached? %>
      <span class="thumb"><img src="<%= public_file_preview_path(project.user.handle, project.slug,
                                                                 thumb.node_id, "thumbnail") %>"
                               alt="" loading="lazy"></span>
    <% else %>
      <span class="thumb project-thumb-empty" aria-hidden="true">📦</span>
    <% end %>
  <% end %>
  <h3 class="card-title">
    <%= link_to project.name, public_project_path(project.user.handle, project.slug) %>
  </h3>
  <span class="muted">by <%= link_to "@#{project.user.handle}", public_user_path(project.user.handle) %></span>
  <% if project.description.present? %>
    <p class="muted card-blurb"><%= truncate(project.description, length: 160) %></p>
  <% end %>
  <% if project.tags.any? %>
    <div class="tag-chips">
      <% project.tags.sort_by(&:name).each do |t| %>
        <%= link_to t.name, public_explore_path(tag: t.name), class: "tag-chip" %>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  <% end %>
  <time class="muted card-time" datetime="<%= project.updated_at.iso8601 %>">
    <%= project.updated_at.strftime("%Y-%m-%d") %>
  </time>
</article>
